  "post": {
    "caption": "Monopoly's dice once had diamond spots. Sidney Mobell was a jeweler in San Francisco, and each year he made a jeweled everyday object to stand out. He once made a gold sardine can, and a gold mousetrap with a diamond cheese wedge. In 1988, he heard about the World Monopoly Tournament in London, so he built a Monopoly set in gold. The board is gold plated, and the pieces are solid gold. Rubies and sapphires top the houses and hotels. Guinness lists it as the most expensive Monopoly set, and the Smithsonian keeps it in a gem vault. Its dice spots are 42 full cut diamonds.",
